+### Protocol-v2 pairing commit (implemented; runtime verification pending)
+
+The v2 flow supersedes the earlier `PAIRING_CONFIRMED` proposal. The host
+verifies the device's PAKE share and sends `PAIRING_RESULT` with its directional
+confirmation. The device verifies that proof, waits for the operator's explicit
+Allow action, and sends `PAIRING_COMMIT` with its withheld directional
+confirmation. The host verifies it, atomically commits the new record and any
+cleanup-token revocations, then returns `PAIRING_COMMIT_RESULT` with the new
+revocation token. Android stores the host pin only after this acknowledgement.
+
+This is a three-message authenticated commit after `PAIRING_START` and
+`PAIRING_SUBMIT`; it is not a server-side two-phase commit across both durable
+stores. If the host commits but the final acknowledgement is lost, the host may
+retain a paired record while the device has not saved its pin. The recovery path
+is to retry pairing or remove the orphaned record. An idempotent transaction
+identifier/status-recovery message remains future work.
 
